  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules impose strict incident reporting (S1) and an 8% market-restriction threshold for the 55°C test with corrective action above 5% (S2). Remote shut-off retrofit is set at six years with a feasibility escape (S3), fire suppression at 36 months (S4), and a mandatory 8/100k recall trigger with open regulator-approved remedies and immediate notices (S5). Overall S1 is safe, S2 and S5 are weakened, and S3/S4 are acceptable."
